# ── Rust build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the workspace root has a target/; the leading slash keeps a
# future crate or directory literally named `target` trackable.
/target/
# The vendored submodule builds into its own target/ when examples are
# run from inside it.
/vendor/*/target/

# rustfmt / rustc leftovers
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This workspace ships binaries (wipemark,
# wipemark-cli) and pins gpui by git rev — a reproducible resolve is the
# whole point. Only the backup file cargo writes on `cargo update` is
# ignored.
Cargo.lock.bak

# ── llama.cpp source ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fetched at the pinned commit by crates/wipemark-llama-sys/vendor/fetch.sh
# and consumed only by the `native` build. A build input reproduced from
# the pin (PIN.md), not source this repository maintains.
/crates/wipemark-llama-sys/vendor/llama.cpp/

# ── Local spec / design drops (ssd-docs) ─────────────────────────────
# Watchword-sourced specs and working design documents land here so they
# sit next to the code without ever being committed. Anything durable
# belongs in docs/ instead; the canonical copy of a spec is its
# Watchword key.
/ssd-docs/

# ── Agent + editor state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Product runtime data ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Downloaded GGUF weights and partial downloads. In normal operation
# these live under the OS data dir (see wipemark-models::layout), but a
# dev run with WIPEMARK_DATA_DIR pointed at the repo would drop them
# here — a multi-GB commit is not the way to find that out.
/models/
*.gguf
*.partial

# The prompt bench's raw records and judgements (texts included) under a
# run's results directory — e.g. bench/run-voice.sh's voice-<date>/. A
# run's tables.md and summary.json are what may be committed
# (docs/architecture/prompt-bench.md).
/crates/wipemark-pipeline/bench/results/*/runs/
/crates/wipemark-pipeline/bench/results/*/judge.jsonl

# Config / queue / history written by the app or CLI during development.
*.log
/config.toml
/presets.toml
/queue.json
/history.jsonl

# ── The regression over real files (scripts/regress.py, golden/README.md) ──
# The owner's pictures, unpacked, and the files derived from them: named
# by golden/manifest.json, never committed (D493). A run's folder is a
# report of the moment; the baseline under golden/baseline/ is committed.
/golden/cache/
# Another corpus folder's (`regress.py --golden golden/<set>`, E12-R12).
/golden/*/cache/
/reports/regress-*/

# ── The restoration bench (scripts/bench/README.md, E12-R5) ─────────────
# A run's backgrounds, composites, variants and results: generated from
# bench/manifest.json (and, for the photo group, the owner's photographs,
# which never enter git — D493). The manifest is committed; a run is not.
/bench/out/

# ── Font Awesome Free staging (icon curation) ────────────────────────
# The corpus is pulled into dev-staging/ to promote single glyphs into
# apps/wipemark-app/assets/icons/. None of it is committed:
# node_modules/ is large and exactly reproducible from package.json,
# an unpacked tarball is the same thing by another road, and
# package-lock.json records the resolved registry URL. The build reads
# only the promoted SVGs, which are committed. See
# docs/architecture/icons.md.
/dev-staging/node_modules/
/dev-staging/fontawesome-free/
/dev-staging/package-lock.json

# ── Packaging output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/dist/
/dist-next/
*.dmg
*.AppImage
*.deb

# ── Scratch clones / upstream reference checkouts ────────────────────
# Third-party repositories cloned for reference (e.g. the
# watermarks-remover survey in docs/sdd/). Read-only, never vendored:
# vendoring goes through .gitmodules so the rev is pinned and the
# licence is recorded in NOTICE.
/tmp/

# ── The Grok chain (scripts/grok/run.sh, E12-R close-out) ──────────────
# A run's folder: stage 0's copy, the ZIPs for Watchword (the owner's
# captures, never committed — D493), stage 1's maps, the calibrations,
# the bench. What is committed is the manifest and the stage-0 table.
/reports/grok-*/

# The Linux builder's pinned tools (ci/linux-builder/fetch-tools.sh): downloaded
# and checked against ci/linux-builder/tools.sha256, never committed.
/ci/linux-builder/vendor/

# ── The product website (scripts/site/build.sh) ───────────────────────
# site/dist/ is assembled from site/ and media/out/ on every build and
# deployed as it is; the sources are what is committed.
/site/dist/

# ── Generated media (media/README.md) ──────────────────────────────────
# Screenshots, clips, the video and the site's icons, made by the tools in
# media/; regenerated, never committed (the owner, 2026-10-16).
/media/out/
